        "original_id": "1aed0824-de30-5ae6-9a7e-302a424ad859",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: University of Washington, Texas Christian University, University of California Riverside\n- People: Theodore Garland, Jr., Raymond B. Huey, Addison Clark, Randolph Clark\n- Roles: editor-in-chief\n- Places: Seattle, Washington, Fort Worth, Texas\n- Topics: university founding, postdoctoral training, academic journal leadership\n\nFacts:\n- The University of Washington was established in 1861 as a large public flagship research university in Seattle, Washington.\n- Texas Christian University was established in 1873 in Fort Worth, Texas, by Addison Clark and Randolph Clark as AddRan Male & Female College.\n- Theodore Garland, Jr. completed postdoctoral training at the University of Washington with Raymond B. Huey.\n- Theodore Garland, Jr. of the University of California, Riverside is the current editor-in-chief of Physiological and Biochemical Zoology.",
